                <pb facs="0137" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7661/5.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Beaupré to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-08-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Beaupré informs Mr. Root that the shipment of deviled ham referred to in his
                    telegram of the 19th ultimo has been again analyzed by the Government, found to
                    contain no boric acid, and passed.)</p>
            </div>
